mc(2, 'household', 'Roquefort cheese is ripened by', 'growing specific fungi on it, which give it a flavour', ['Propionibacterium', 'Lactobacillus only', 'Rhizobium'], 'Different cheeses get their flavour, texture and taste from the specific microbes used. Roquefort uses fungi.');
mc(2, 'industrial', 'Alcoholic drinks such as wine and beer are produced by the fermentation by', '<i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>', ['<i>Aspergillus niger</i>', '<i>Acetobacter aceti</i>', '<i>Clostridium butylicum</i>'], 'S. cerevisiae is also called brewer\'s yeast.');
mc(2, 'industrial', 'Which of these is a bioactive molecule used as an immunosuppressive agent?', 'Cyclosporin A', ['Streptokinase', 'Lipase', 'Pectinase'], 'Cyclosporin A, produced by the fungus <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>, is used in organ transplants.');
mc(2, 'industrial', 'The microbe that is the source of statins is', '<i>Monascus purpureus</i>', ['<i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>', '<i>Streptococcus</i>', '<i>Penicillium notatum</i>'], 'Statins from the yeast <i>Monascus purpureus</i> lower blood cholesterol.');
mc(2, 'sewage', 'In sewage treatment, the removal of floating debris and grit by filtration and sedimentation is part of', 'primary treatment', ['secondary treatment', 'anaerobic digestion', 'biogas formation'], 'Primary treatment is physical. Secondary treatment is biological.');
