asr(3, 'sewage', 'High BOD means more polluted water.', 'More organic matter needs more oxygen for microbial breakdown.', 0, 'High organic load means more oxygen used by microbes.');
asr(3, 'sewage', 'Activated sludge is partly returned to the aeration tank.', 'It serves as the inoculum of microbes.', 0, 'The returned flocs act as a starter of microbes in the aeration tank.');
asr(3, 'biofertilisers', 'Rhizobium is used in the cultivation of pulses.', 'Rhizobium forms nodules on the roots of leguminous plants.', 0, 'The nodules host the bacterium that fixes N<sub>2</sub> for the legume.');
asr(3, 'industrial', 'Statins are used to lower blood cholesterol.', 'Statins competitively inhibit the enzyme that synthesises cholesterol.', 0, 'By competing for the active site, statins slow cholesterol production.');
stm(3, 'sewage', 'Primary treatment of sewage is a physical process.', 'Secondary treatment is biological.', 0, 'Both are correct.');
stm(3, 'biogas', 'Biogas is mainly methane.', 'Biogas is made by aerobic bacteria.', 2, 'It is made by anaerobic methanogens.');
stm(3, 'biocontrol', 'Baculoviruses are broad spectrum insecticides.', 'Baculoviruses are species-specific.', 3, 'They are narrow spectrum. Statement I is wrong.');
stm(3, 'industrial', 'Yeast makes ethanol.', 'Yeast also makes CO<sub>2</sub>.', 0, 'Both products come from fermentation by yeast.');
match(3, 'sewage', 'xm2', 'Stage and what happens', ['A. Primary treatment', 'B. Secondary treatment', 'C. Sludge digester', 'D. Final effluent'], ['p. Aerobic microbes grow as flocs and BOD falls', 'q. Biogas is formed', 'r. Physical removal of debris and grit', 's. Released into rivers or streams'], 'A-r, B-p, C-q, D-s', ['A-p, B-r, C-q, D-s', 'A-r, B-p, C-s, D-q', 'A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s'], 'Primary is physical, secondary is aerobic and biological, the digester forms biogas and the effluent goes to rivers.');
match(3, 'biocontrol', 'xm3', 'Biocontrol agent and the target', ['A. Ladybird', 'B. Dragonfly', 'C. <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>', 'D. Trichoderma'], ['p. Aphids', 'q. Mosquitoes', 'r. Butterfly caterpillars', 's. Plant pathogens'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'Ladybirds eat aphids, dragonflies eat mosquitoes, Bt kills caterpillars and Trichoderma controls plant pathogens.');
pass('xp1', 'Passage: a village with a dung problem', 'A village keeps many cattle. The dung is dumped near homes and causes foul smell. An organisation sets up a concrete tank where dung is mixed with water to form a slurry and a floating drum is placed on it. After some days the drum rises and the gas is piped to the kitchen. The spent slurry is taken out through an outlet.');
pq('xp1', 3, 'biogas', 'The gas which burns in the kitchen is mostly', 'methane', ['oxygen', 'carbon dioxide', 'nitrogen'], 'Methane is the main part of biogas.');
pq('xp1', 4, 'biogas', 'The organisms producing the gas are', 'methanogens such as <i>Methanobacterium</i>', ['aerobic yeasts', 'cyanobacteria', 'LAB'], 'Methanogens grow anaerobically on the dung slurry.');
pq('xp1', 4, 'biogas', 'The spent slurry can be used as', 'a manure or fertiliser', ['a fuel gas', 'an antibiotic', 'a food for humans'], 'The spent slurry is rich in nutrients and is used as manure.');
nat(3, 'sewage', 'Raw sewage has a BOD of 280 mg/L. After treatment the BOD is 14 mg/L. What percentage of the BOD has been removed?', 95, '(280 - 14)/280 × 100 = 266/280 × 100 = 95 per cent.', '%');
nat(3, 'household', 'A starter has 1 million LAB per mL. The bacteria double every 30 minutes. How many million LAB per mL are expected after 3 hours?', 64, '3 hours = 6 doublings. 1 × 2<sup>6</sup> = 64 million.', 'million per mL', 'Count 6 doublings, not 3.');

// L4
mc(4, 'household', 'Which of the following correctly explains why milk curdles after LAB act on it?', 'Lactic acid lowers the pH and coagulates and partially digests milk proteins', ['Lactic acid raises the pH', 'Yeast makes CO<sub>2</sub>', 'Lactose becomes fat'], 'LAB make lactic acid from lactose. The acid coagulates the milk protein casein.');
mc(4, 'household', 'Large holes in Swiss cheese are due to', 'CO<sub>2</sub> produced by <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i>', ['air bubbles pumped in', 'yeast fermentation', 'methane from archaea'], 'The bacterium is a large producer of CO<sub>2</sub>, which forms the holes.');
mc(4, 'industrial', 'Which statement is correct about distillation in making alcoholic drinks?', 'Whisky, brandy and rum are obtained by distilling the fermented broth, but wine and beer are not distilled', ['Wine and beer are distilled but rum is not', 'No drink needs distillation', 'All drinks are distilled'], 'Wine and beer are produced without distillation. Whisky, brandy and rum need distillation.');
mc(4, 'industrial', 'Which of the following is true about fermentors (bioreactors) used in industry?', 'They are large vessels in which microbes are grown on a large scale to get products', ['They are used only for sewage', 'They are small glass flasks', 'They produce no heat'], 'Industrial products such as antibiotics are made in large fermentors.');
mc(4, 'industrial', 'The enzyme streptokinase is made by', '<i>Streptococcus</i> and modified through genetic engineering', ['<i>Monascus</i>', '<i>Trichoderma</i>', '<i>Aspergillus</i>'], 'Streptokinase from the bacterium <i>Streptococcus</i> was modified by genetic engineering and is used as a clot buster.');
mc(4, 'industrial', 'Bottled fruit juices are clear because', 'pectinases and proteases are added to remove cloudy materials', ['they are filtered through sand only', 'lipases are added', 'they are fermented by yeast'], 'Pectinases and proteases break down pectin and proteins that make the juice turbid.');
mc(4, 'sewage', 'In the aeration tank, the organic matter falls because', 'aerobic microbes use it for growth and respiration while air is supplied', ['the tank is closed', 'the tank contains chemicals only', 'methane is produced'], 'Aerobic microbes oxidise the organic matter and so BOD falls significantly.');
mc(4, 'sewage', 'In the anaerobic sludge digester, the microbes break down', 'the bacteria and fungi in the sludge', ['sand', 'metal particles', 'only oxygen'], 'Anaerobic bacteria digest the bacteria and fungi in the sludge and produce biogas.');
mc(4, 'sewage', 'Which of the following correctly orders the steps in sewage treatment?', 'Filtration and sedimentation, aeration, settling of flocs, anaerobic digestion of sludge', ['Aeration, filtration, digestion, settling', 'Digestion, aeration, filtration', 'Settling, filtration, digestion'], 'Primary treatment (physical) comes first, then aeration with flocs, then settling gives activated sludge and the sludge goes to digesters.');
mc(4, 'biogas', 'Which of the following statements about biogas is correct?', 'Methanogens break down cellulosic material into methane', ['Biogas needs oxygen', 'Biogas has no methane', 'Methanogens are aerobic'], 'Methanogens like <i>Methanobacterium</i> grow anaerobically on cellulosic material.');
mc(4, 'biogas', 'In a biogas plant the floating cover keeps rising because', 'gas accumulates beneath it as dung is digested', ['water evaporates', 'dung expands', 'the tank is hot'], 'The gas collects under the cover and lifts it.');
mc(4, 'biocontrol', 'A farmer wants to avoid harming beneficial insects. A good choice is', 'a baculovirus, because it has a narrow host range', ['a broad-spectrum pesticide', 'a chemical weedicide', 'a fertiliser'], 'Species-specific control is desirable when beneficial insects are to be conserved, as in IPM.');
mc(4, 'biocontrol', 'Biological control is attractive because it', 'has no negative effects on plants, mammals, birds and fishes when used properly', ['kills every insect', 'is a chemical process', 'raises soil salinity'], 'Species-specific agents do not harm non-target organisms.', 'Biocontrol agents are not totally risk-free but they are more selective.');
mc(4, 'biofertilisers', 'Which of the following is a symbiotic nitrogen-fixer?', '<i>Rhizobium</i>', ['<i>Azospirillum</i>', '<i>Azotobacter</i>', '<i>Oscillatoria</i>'], 'Rhizobium lives in the root nodules of legumes.');
mc(4, 'biofertilisers', 'Which pair is correct regarding biofertilisers?', 'Anabaena: cyanobacterium for paddy fields; Glomus: fungus for phosphorus uptake', ['Anabaena: fungus; Glomus: bacterium', 'Azotobacter: fungus; Rhizobium: free-living', 'Nostoc: virus; Oscillatoria: bacterium'], 'Anabaena is a cyanobacterium and Glomus a fungus forming mycorrhiza.');
mc(4, 'biofertilisers', 'Why is the use of biofertilisers considered better than chemical fertilisers for the long term?', 'They enrich the soil nutrients and help in sustainable farming without pollution', ['They give crops in a day', 'They are chemicals', 'They contain antibiotics'], 'Biofertilisers reduce the dependence on chemical fertilisers and are less polluting.');
asr(4, 'industrial', 'Whisky is produced by fermentation followed by distillation.', 'Distillation is needed to separate and concentrate the alcohol from the fermented broth.', 0, 'The fermented broth has limited alcohol. Distilling it gives the spirit, so R explains A.');
asr(4, 'sewage', 'The secondary treatment of sewage is also called biological treatment.', 'It uses aerobic microbes to reduce BOD.', 0, 'Microbes do the work, so it is biological.');
asr(4, 'biogas', 'Anaerobic conditions are needed for biogas production.', 'Methanogens are anaerobic.', 0, 'Methanogens do not grow in the presence of oxygen.');
asr(4, 'biocontrol', 'Bt spores are sprayed on brassica plants to kill caterpillars.', 'The toxin protein is released in the gut of the larvae that eat the spores.', 0, 'The spores are eaten, and the toxin acts in the alkaline gut.');
asr(4, 'biofertilisers', 'Mycorrhiza-infected plants have a better tolerance to salinity.', 'The fungus is a pathogen of the plant.', 2, 'The fungus is a symbiont, not a pathogen. R is false.');
stm(4, 'industrial', 'Cyclosporin A is an immunosuppressant.', 'Cyclosporin A is produced by a bacterium.', 2, 'It is produced by the fungus <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>.');
stm(4, 'industrial', 'Statins competitively inhibit the enzyme for cholesterol synthesis.', 'Statins are obtained from <i>Monascus purpureus</i>.', 0, 'Both are correct.');
stm(4, 'sewage', 'Flocs are formed in the settling tank by aerobic bacteria.', 'Primary sludge is formed in the aeration tank.', 1, 'Flocs form in the aeration tank, not the settling tank. Primary sludge forms in the primary settling tank. Both are incorrect.');
stm(4, 'biofertilisers', 'Anabaena, Nostoc and Oscillatoria are cyanobacteria.', 'Cyanobacteria are heterotrophs.', 2, 'They are autotrophic, so Statement II is wrong.');
stm(4, 'biocontrol', 'Dragonflies are used for control of mosquitoes.', 'Ladybirds control aphids.', 0, 'Both are correct examples of biocontrol.');
mc(4, 'industrial', 'How many of the following are correct? (a) Lipases are used in detergents. (b) Streptokinase lowers blood cholesterol. (c) Pectinases clarify juices. (d) Cyclosporin A is an antibiotic.', 'Two', ['One', 'Three', 'Four'], '(a) and (c) are correct. (b) is wrong: statins lower cholesterol and streptokinase dissolves clots. (d) is wrong: cyclosporin A suppresses immunity.', 'Do not mix up statins and streptokinase.', 'statements');
mc(4, 'biofertilisers', 'How many of these are free-living nitrogen-fixing bacteria: Azotobacter, Azospirillum, Rhizobium, Glomus, Trichoderma?', 'Two', ['One', 'Three', 'Four'], 'Azotobacter and Azospirillum are free-living N<sub>2</sub> fixers. Rhizobium is symbiotic, and Glomus and Trichoderma are fungi.', 'Rhizobium fixes nitrogen only in nodules.', 'statements');
