match(4, 'industrial', 'xm5', 'Product and its use', ['A. Lipase', 'B. Pectinase', 'C. Streptokinase', 'D. Cyclosporin A'], ['p. Detergents', 'q. Clarifying juices', 'r. Clot buster', 's. Immunosuppression'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'Lipase for oily stains, pectinase for juices, streptokinase for clots and cyclosporin A in transplants.');
match(4, 'industrial', 'xm6', 'Drink and how it is made', ['A. Wine', 'B. Beer', 'C. Whisky', 'D. Rum'], ['p. Fermentation without distillation', 'q. Fermentation followed by distillation'], 'A-p, B-p, C-q, D-q', ['A-q, B-p, C-p, D-q', 'A-p, B-q, C-q, D-p', 'A-q, B-q, C-p, D-p'], 'Wine and beer are not distilled while whisky and rum are distilled.');
pass('xp2', 'Passage: a sewage plant', 'In a town\'s plant, the raw sewage first passes through screens and a grit chamber. The clear liquid goes to a large tank where air is pumped in. After some time the liquid goes to a settling tank. Some of the sediment is sent back to the aeration tank and the rest to a closed tank without air. The BOD of the incoming sewage is 300 mg/L and of the final effluent 15 mg/L.');
pq('xp2', 3, 'sewage', 'The sediment that is partly returned to the aeration tank is', 'activated sludge', ['primary sludge', 'biogas', 'grit'], 'It carries flocs that act as an inoculum.');
pq('xp2', 4, 'sewage', 'The percentage reduction of BOD across the plant is', '95 per cent', ['5 per cent', '85 per cent', '99 per cent'], '(300 - 15)/300 × 100 = 95.');
pq('xp2', 4, 'sewage', 'In the closed tank, the main process is', 'anaerobic digestion producing biogas', ['aeration and flocculation', 'filtration', 'chlorination'], 'Anaerobic bacteria digest the sludge and give biogas.');
pass('xp3', 'Passage: a farmer\'s choices', 'A farmer has a paddy field, a pulse field and an orchard on poor phosphorus soil. He also has a cabbage field with caterpillars. He wants to avoid chemical fertilisers and insecticides as far as possible.');
pq('xp3', 3, 'biofertilisers', 'For the paddy field, a good biofertiliser is', 'cyanobacteria such as <i>Anabaena</i>', ['<i>Rhizobium</i>', '<i>Glomus</i>', '<i>Trichoderma</i>'], 'Cyanobacteria fix nitrogen and add organic matter in flooded fields.');
pq('xp3', 3, 'biofertilisers', 'For the pulse field, a good choice is', '<i>Rhizobium</i>', ['<i>Anabaena</i>', '<i>Penicillium</i>', '<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>'], 'Pulses are legumes that form nodules with Rhizobium.');
pq('xp3', 4, 'biocontrol', 'For the caterpillars on cabbage, a biological choice is', '<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> spores', ['<i>Glomus</i>', 'LAB', '<i>Methanobacterium</i>'], 'Bt kills caterpillar larvae when they eat the sprayed spores.');
pq('xp3', 4, 'biofertilisers', 'For the orchard with poor phosphorus soil, the best choice is', 'mycorrhiza such as <i>Glomus</i>', ['<i>Rhizobium</i>', '<i>Azotobacter</i>', '<i>Nostoc</i>'], 'The fungus absorbs phosphorus and passes it to the plant.');
nat(4, 'sewage', 'Raw sewage has BOD 450 mg/L. Primary treatment removes 30 per cent. The secondary treatment then removes 92 per cent of what is left. What is the final BOD in mg/L?', 25.2, 'After primary: 450 × 0.70 = 315. After secondary: 315 × 0.08 = 25.2 mg/L.', 'mg/L', 'Secondary removes 92 per cent; 8 per cent remains.', 0.1);
nat(4, 'sewage', 'A plant discharges 3000 L of effluent per hour with BOD 15 mg/L. How many grams of oxygen would microbes need per day to break down the organic matter in this effluent?', 1080, 'Per hour: 3000 × 15 = 45000 mg = 45 g. Per day: 45 × 24 = 1080 g.', 'g', 'Convert mg to g.');
nat(4, 'household', 'Among Lactobacillus, Streptococcus, Clostridium, Monascus, Trichoderma and Propionibacterium, how many are bacteria?', 4, 'Lactobacillus, Streptococcus, Clostridium and Propionibacterium are bacteria. Monascus and Trichoderma are fungi.', null, 'Count only bacteria.');

