mc(5, 'industrial', 'Which one of the following is a correctly matched pair of microbe with its group?', '<i>Monascus purpureus</i>: fungus', ['<i>Streptococcus</i>: fungus', '<i>Trichoderma</i>: bacterium', '<i>Propionibacterium</i>: virus'], 'Monascus (yeast) and Trichoderma are fungi, and Streptococcus and Propionibacterium are bacteria.');
mc(5, 'industrial', 'Which of the following microbes is used for two different products in NCERT?', '<i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> for bread and alcoholic drinks', ['<i>Monascus</i> for bread', '<i>Clostridium</i> for citric acid', '<i>Acetobacter</i> for streptokinase'], 'Baker\'s yeast and brewer\'s yeast are the same species used in dough and in fermented beverages.');
mc(5, 'industrial', 'In the textbook account which statement about antibiotics is correct?', 'Penicillin was discovered by Fleming in 1928 but its full potential was established later by Chain and Florey', ['Penicillin was discovered by Chain and Florey in 1928', 'Fleming got the Nobel Prize alone', 'Penicillin was discovered in 1945'], 'The three scientists got the Nobel Prize in 1945.', 'Observation and establishing usefulness are different steps.');
mc(5, 'sewage', 'The reason that BOD of effluent leaving the secondary treatment is much lower than the raw sewage is that', 'aerobic microbes used much of the organic matter', ['the sewage was diluted by air', 'oxygen was removed', 'the effluent was heated'], 'The consumption of organic matter by microbes is what lowers the BOD.');
mc(5, 'sewage', 'An effluent is released into a river without secondary treatment. The most likely effect is', 'a fall of dissolved oxygen as the microbes use it and fish may die', ['a rise of dissolved oxygen', 'no change', 'a fall in pH to 0'], 'High BOD effluent in the river causes oxygen shortage as microbes act on the organic matter.');
mc(5, 'biogas', 'Which of the following is the correct pair of facts about biogas?', 'Methanogens grow anaerobically and the gas is mostly methane with CO<sub>2</sub> and H<sub>2</sub>S', ['Methanogens need air and the gas is all CO<sub>2</sub>', 'Biogas has no methane', 'Methanogens grow on mineral ores'], 'Methanogens are anaerobic and the gas is a mixture with methane as the main component.');
mc(5, 'biocontrol', 'A scientist discovers a virus that infects only one species of caterpillar. Which of its features would be most valued in IPM?', 'Its narrow host range, which spares beneficial insects', ['Its ability to kill every insect', 'Its ability to infect humans', 'Its ability to infect plants'], 'Species specificity is the key advantage of baculoviruses in IPM.');
mc(5, 'biofertilisers', 'Which of the following is a benefit of mycorrhiza other than phosphorus uptake?', 'Resistance to root-borne pathogens and tolerance to salinity and drought', ['Fixing atmospheric nitrogen like Rhizobium', 'Making antibiotics for humans', 'Producing flowers'], 'Mycorrhiza-infected plants grow better, resist root pathogens, and tolerate salinity and drought.');
mc(5, 'biofertilisers', 'Which of the following correctly states the difference between Rhizobium and Azotobacter?', 'Rhizobium fixes nitrogen in association with legume roots, Azotobacter fixes it while free-living in the soil', ['Rhizobium is a fungus', 'Azotobacter lives in nodules', 'Both live only in water'], 'The first is symbiotic and the second is free-living.');
asr(5, 'sewage', 'Anaerobic sludge digesters need no air pump.', 'The microbes that work there grow in the absence of oxygen.', 0, 'The anaerobic bacteria are inhibited by oxygen, so no aeration is needed.');
asr(5, 'industrial', 'Fleming got the Nobel Prize for penicillin alone.', 'Chain and Florey established the effectiveness of penicillin.', 3, 'Fleming shared the prize in 1945 with Chain and Florey, so A is false. R is true.');
asr(5, 'biofertilisers', 'Azotobacter is useful for non-legumes.', 'Azotobacter fixes nitrogen as a free-living organism in soil.', 0, 'It does not need a legume host, so it is useful for cereals and other crops.');
stm(5, 'biocontrol', 'Ladybirds control aphids and dragonflies control mosquitoes.', 'Bt acts only after it is eaten by the larvae.', 0, 'Both are correct.');
stm(5, 'sewage', 'Both Ganga and Yamuna Action Plans were launched by the Ministry of Environment and Forests.', 'They aim to save the major rivers of the country from pollution.', 0, 'Both are correct.');
stm(5, 'industrial', 'Citric acid is produced by <i>Aspergillus niger</i>, lactic acid by <i>Lactobacillus</i>.', 'Butyric acid is produced by <i>Acetobacter aceti</i>.', 2, 'Acetobacter aceti makes acetic acid; butyric acid comes from Clostridium butylicum.');
mc(5, 'sewage', 'How many of the following are correct? (a) Flocs form in the aeration tank. (b) Activated sludge is returned in part. (c) Primary treatment is microbial. (d) Effluent of secondary treatment is released into rivers.', 'Three', ['Two', 'Four', 'One'], '(a), (b) and (d) are correct. (c) is wrong: primary treatment is physical.', null, 'statements');
mc(5, 'industrial', 'How many of these produce a product used in medicine: Trichoderma polysporum, Monascus purpureus, Streptococcus, Penicillium notatum, Aspergillus niger?', 'Four', ['Three', 'Five', 'Two'], 'The first four produce cyclosporin A, statins, streptokinase and penicillin. Aspergillus niger is used for citric acid.', 'The citric acid producer is not a medicine.', 'statements');
match(5, 'industrial', 'xm7', 'Microbe and its group', ['A. <i>Monascus purpureus</i>', 'B. <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i>', 'C. <i>Nostoc</i>', 'D. Baculovirus'], ['p. Fungus', 'q. Bacterium', 'r. Cyanobacterium', 's. Virus'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'Monascus is a yeast, Propionibacterium a bacterium, Nostoc a cyanobacterium and baculovirus a virus.');
match(5, 'sewage', 'xm8', 'Item and the body or people linked', ['A. Biogas technology in India', 'B. Ganga Action Plan', 'C. Nobel Prize 1945 for penicillin', 'D. First antibiotic noticed in 1928'], ['p. IARI and KVIC', 'q. Ministry of Environment and Forests', 'r. Fleming, Chain and Florey', 's. Fleming'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'IARI and KVIC developed biogas technology, the MoEF launched the river plans, three scientists shared the Nobel Prize and Fleming noticed the mould in 1928.');
nat(5, 'sewage', 'A plant treats 5000 L of raw sewage per hour with BOD 280 mg/L, and it reduces the BOD by 95 per cent. How many grams of oxygen demand are removed per day?', 31920, 'BOD removed per litre = 0.95 × 280 = 266 mg/L. Per hour = 5000 × 266 = 1,330,000 mg = 1330 g. Per day = 1330 × 24 = 31,920 g.', 'g', 'Use only the removed part (95 per cent).');

